{"type":"message","id":"7360428c","parentId":"f5830301","timestamp":"2026-05-20T01:18:18.055Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The error code 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker rejected\" - the worker itself is rejecting the request, possibly because of CORS or some other issue. Or maybe the send endpoint has a different issue - maybe it's a different error type.\n\nWait, when I tried with the `Authorization: Bearer` header it returned \"Unauthorized\", but with `X-API-Key` it returns error 1101. That suggests X-API-Key is accepted but there's something else wrong.\n\nLet me try different approaches:\n1. Maybe the body needs `text` field instead\n2. Maybe the URL is different\n3. Maybe there's a rate limit\n\nLet me try a simple message first to see if it even works.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-10c4c924-9f8c-4ded-a0f3-6adf178876b5","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test 01:15 UTC\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":21519,"output":245,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21876,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779239885175,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8691bd78-3776-46e2-9040-a15cc882cddb"}}
