{"type":"message","id":"105c0a31","parentId":"d7369e08","timestamp":"2026-05-20T01:18:34.539Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting 1101 with `X-API-Key`. When I used `Authorization: Bearer` I got \"Unauthorized\", but with `X-API-Key` I get 1101 which is a different error.\n\nMaybe the send endpoint requires a different auth method. Let me try without any auth to see what happens, or with a different header format.\n\nActually, 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker execution failed\" - the worker itself is crashing or throwing an error. This might mean the endpoint itself has a bug or there's something wrong with the request format.\n\nLet me try with `message` field instead of `content`, or maybe the endpoint expects `text`.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-903e79bb-4961-4ee3-bc3d-7ef8c37bd95b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test 01:15 UTC\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":21787,"output":234,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22133,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779239898203,"responseId":"chatcmpl-ce827c1e-4a9a-46b8-818d-dac87817d94c"}}
