{"type":"message","id":"4e890e5e","parentId":"67cf9933","timestamp":"2026-05-20T01:19:08.065Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So with `X-API-Key` + `content` I get error 1101 (worker rejected), but with `Authorization: Bearer` + `content` I get \"Unauthorized\". This suggests the `X-API-Key` header with `content` field is the closest to working - the auth is accepted but there's something else wrong.\n\nMaybe the issue is the `content` field name. Let me try other field names like `text`, `msg`, or `body`.\n\nActually wait - when I used `X-API-Key` with `{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"...\"}` I got error 1101. When I used `X-API-Key` with `{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"...\"}` I also got 1101. \n\nThe 1101 error from Cloudflare Workers suggests the worker itself is crashing, which could mean the request body format is wrong or missing required fields. Let me try switching back to `message` as the field name - that's what the other agent used in its POST request, so maybe that's what the endpoint expects.\n\nLooking at the 1101 error more carefully, this is a Cloudflare Workers error code for \"Worker exceeded resources\" or a script error, not an HTTP error. Since the auth is passing with `X-API-Key`, the issue might be in how the body is being processed - maybe the endpoint expects a different format or I need to try with `text` field instead.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-5b4fc002-bd32-4c44-8f37-ff732416728d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -v -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' 2>&1 | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":22039,"output":401,"cacheRead